option.BLOOM_RADIUS=Glow radius
option.BLOOM_QUALITY=Glow quality §e[?]
option.BLOOM_QUALITY.comment=Fast blurs at quarter resolution with fewer samples; Fancy uses more samples for smoother glow
value.BLOOM_QUALITY.0=§aFast
value.BLOOM_QUALITY.1=§eBalanced
value.BLOOM_QUALITY.2=§cFancy
option.BLOOM_SATURATION=Glow saturation §e[?]
option.BLOOM_SATURATION.comment=Above 1 makes the glow color more vivid than the source texture; below 1 washes it out
option.BLOOM_SKY=Sky glow §e[?]
option.BLOOM_SKY.comment=Lets the sun and bright sky glow; blocks are unaffected - they glow only through real light emission
option.BLOOM_PIXEL_THRESHOLD=Glow pixel cutoff §e[?]
option.BLOOM_PIXEL_THRESHOLD.comment=Base brightness a pixel of a light-emitting block needs to glow. Flame-bodied blocks (lantern, campfire, torch) use a stricter value, lava and glowstone a lower one. Raise if block bodies glow, lower if flames lose glow
option.BLOOM_EMISSIVE_TEXTURES=Texture pack emissives §e[?]
option.BLOOM_EMISSIVE_TEXTURES.comment=Adds glow to emissive overlay textures from resource packs (rendered fullbright)
option.BLOOM_PARTICLES=Particle glow §e[?]
option.BLOOM_PARTICLES.comment=Bright particles (fire, flames, lava drips) glow. The beacon beam has its own dedicated glow, always on with Glow enabled
screen.COLORED_LIGHT_SCREEN=Colored light
option.COLORED_LIGHT=Colored lighting §e[?]
option.COLORED_LIGHT.comment=Real per-source colored block light: light takes the color of the emitting block (lava orange, soul fire blue, portal purple). Iris only, all dimensions; intensity and range stay vanilla so light never leaks through walls
option.COLORED_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Color intensity §e[?]
option.COLORED_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Higher values carry the light color farther from the source and deepen its saturation; lower values keep colors subtle and close
option.CL_ENTITY_LIGHT=Entity lights §e[?]
option.CL_ENTITY_LIGHT.comment=Light items held by other players and mobs emit colored light, burning entities and flaming arrows glow warm, and blazes, magma cubes, glow squids and allays emit their own light. Requires Entity shadows set to All (Shadows screen)
option.CL_ITEM_LIGHT=Dropped item lights §e[?]
option.CL_ITEM_LIGHT.comment=Dropped light items and item frames holding one (torch, lantern, glowstone...) emit colored light. Requires Entity shadows set to All (Shadows screen)
option.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE=Light color range §e[?]
option.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE.comment=Maximum distance (in blocks) at which light sources feed the colored light field. Automatically capped at half the Volume size; ranges past 64 also need a larger Volume AND a Shadow distance at least twice the range
option.VOXEL_SIZE=Volume size §e[?]
option.VOXEL_SIZE.comment=Width of the colored light voxel volume in blocks - the hard ceiling of light color range. Height doubles past 256. GPU memory and compute cost grow with the square of this value: 64-128 cheap, 256 moderate, 384-512 heavy
option.TORCH_FALLOFF=Block light softness §e[?]
option.TORCH_FALLOFF.comment=Reshapes the vanilla block light curve: above 1 lifts dark corners and smooths the hard distance steps of torch light (works everywhere, no leaking possible); below 1 makes falloff harsher. 1.0 = vanilla curve
option.CL_TRANSITION=Color transition speed §e[?]
option.CL_TRANSITION.comment=How fast surfaces convert between the default warm light and a source's voxel color when a light appears, disappears or enters range. Lower = smoother, slower fade; 1.0 = instant (old behavior)
option.CL_LAVA_TEXTURE=Lava color from texture §e[?]
option.CL_LAVA_TEXTURE.comment=Lava and magma take their light color from the actual texture instead of the Lava & magma palette sliders, following resource packs that recolor lava (mcmeta). Off = fixed palette color
option.CL_FALLOFF=Falloff softness §e[?]
option.CL_FALLOFF.comment=How softly colored light decays with distance. Higher values let the light travel farther and make the colors of two nearby sources overlap and merge over a wider band; lower values keep each color tight around its own source

